          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em topological vector bundle
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"} vector bundle
            in the context of
            = succeed ":" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topology"} topology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
            over a given
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
          %p
            For more survey and motivation see at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"} vector bundle
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topology"} topology
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differentiable+vector+bundle"} differentiable vector bundle
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+vector+bundle"} algebraic vector bundle
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            We first give the more abstract definiton in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+categories"} slice categories
            (def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologicalVectorBundleInTermsOfSliceCategories"}
            below) and then unwind this to the traditional definition (def
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologicalVectorBundle"}
            below).
          %p In the following
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                is either the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+field"} topological field
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi k
                          %mo =
                          %mi ℝ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k = \mathbb{R}
                    of
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
                %li
                  %p
                    or
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi k
                          %mo =
                          %mi ℂ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k = \mathbb{C}
                    of
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+numbers"} complex numbers
              %p
                equipped with the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+space"} Euclidean
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+topology"} metric topology
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
                means
                = succeed "." do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+dimensional+vector+space"} finite dimensional vector space
          %h3#InTermsOfSliceCategories In terms of slice categories
          #TopologicalVectorBundleInTermsOfSliceCategories.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              %strong (topological vector bundles in terms of slice categories)
            %p
              Write
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Top
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in Top
              a space, write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Top
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top_{/X}
              for its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+category"} slice category
              over
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+product"} Cartesian product
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Top
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top_{/X}
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+product"} fiber product
              over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Top
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %msub
                        %mo ×
                        %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-) \times_X (-)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi k
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi Top
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [X \times k \to X] \in Top_{/X}
              is canonically a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization"} internal
              to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Top
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top_{/X}
            %p
              A
              %em topological vector bundle
              over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Top
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in Top
              is
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  an
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi E
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mi π
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [E \overset{\pi}{\to} X]
                  of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Top
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top_{/X}
              %li
                %p
                  with the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure"} structure
                  of an
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                          %mo ×
                          %mi k
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \times k
                  = succeed "-object" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization"} internal
                  to
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi Top
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                              %mi X
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top_{/X}
                %ol
                  %li
                    %p
                      a
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
