                        %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \subset X\}_{i \in I}
              (for if they are not, then both are cohomologous to cocycles on a joint refinement of the original covers and we may argue with these).
            %p
              Accordingly, by example
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologicalVectorBundleFromCechCocycle"}
              the two bundles
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
