                    E_2 \simeq \left(\underset{i \in I}{\sqcup} (U_i \times k^n) \right) / \left(  \left\{ g_{i j}\right\}_{i,j\in I} \right)
                    \\,.
            %p
              Hence
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^{-1}
              is equivalently a function on this quotient space, and we need to show that as such it is continuous.
            %p
              By the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint+union+space"} disjoint union space
              (the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"} coproduct
              in
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo ×
                    %msup
                      %mi k
                      %mi n
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi f
                          %mi i
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo ×
                    %msup
                      %mi k
                      %mi n
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi ϕ
                          %mi i
                          %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\{ U_i \times k^n \overset{f_i^{-1}}{\to} U_i \times k^n \overset{\phi^1_i}{\to} E_1 \}_{i \in I}
            %p corresponds to a single continuous function of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mi i
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ∘
                    %msubsup
                      %mi f
                      %mi i
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %munder
                      %mo ⊔
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo ×
                    %msup
                      %mi k
                      %mi n
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (\phi^1_i \circ f_i^{-1})_{i \in I}
                    \\;\colon\;
                    \\underset{i \in I}{\sqcup} U_i \times k^n
                    \\longrightarrow
                    E_1
                    \\,.
            %p
              These functions respect the equivalence relation, since for each
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo ∩
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in U_i \cap U_j
              we have
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mi i
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ∘
                    %msubsup
                      %mi f
                      %mi i
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
