                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_n \times_X U_n
              and hence over
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_n
            %p
              Now by the pullback definition of the
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi E
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_n
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pasting+law"} pasting law
              says that for each
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              we have a pullback square of vector bundles of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi E
                              %mrow
                                %mi n
                                %mo +
                                %mn 1
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi h
                                  %mi n
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi E
                              %mi n
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi pb
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mrow
                                %mi n
                                %mo +
                                %mn 1
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mi n
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↘
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↙
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    E_{n+1}
                    \&amp;&amp; \overset{h_n}{\longrightarrow} &amp;&amp;
                    E_n
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; (pb) &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    X_{n+1} &amp;&amp; \longrightarrow &amp;&amp; X_n
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \searrow &amp;&amp; \swarrow
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; X
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              By the nature of pullbacks, the top horizontal function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi h
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h_n
              in this diagram is on each fiber a linear isomorphism. Therefore prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FiberwiseIsoisIsomorphismOfVectorBundles"}
              implies that each
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi h
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h_n
              is in fact an isomorphism of vector bundles over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %p
              By local finiteness, each point
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
              has a neighbourhood
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_x
              such that only a finite number
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi n
                      %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n_x
              of these
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi h
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h_n
              are non-trivial, and so it makes sense to consider the infinite composition
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                    %mo ≔
                    %msub
                      %mi h
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ∘
                    %msub
                      %mi h
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ∘
                    %msub
                      %mi h
                      %mn 3
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi ⋯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    h \coloneqq h_1 \circ h_2 \circ h_3 \circ \cdots
            %p
              understood to be on each
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_x
              the finite composite
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %msub
                      %mi h
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ∘
                    %msub
                      %mi h
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mi x
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    h(x) \coloneqq h_1 \circ \cdots \circ h_{n_x}
                    \\,.
            %p
              Since all the
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi h
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h_k
              are vector bundle isomorphisms, so are all their composites. Thus
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h
              is an isomorphism of the required form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi E
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo ×
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mo ≃
                    %mi E
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo ×
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    h
                    \\;\colon\;
                    E|_{X \times \{0\}}
                    \\overset{\simeq}{\longrightarrow}
                    E|_{X \times \{1\}}
                    \\,.
          #PullbackOfvectorBundlesAlongHomotopicMapsAreIsomorphic.num_cor
            %h6#corollary Corollary
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              be a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/paracompact+Hausdorff+space"} paracompact Hausdorff space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \to Y
              be a topological
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"} vector bundle
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f,g \colon X \to Y
              be two
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+functions"} continuous functions
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi η
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi f
                    %mo →
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta \colon f \to g
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+homotopy"} left homotopy
              between them. Then there is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
              of vector bundles over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              between the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback+of+vector+bundles"} pullback of vector bundles
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              along
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              and along
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mi E
                    %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi g
                      %mo *
                    %mi E
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    f^\ast E \simeq g^\ast E
                    \\,.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_11 Proof
            %p
              By definition, the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+homotopy"} left homotopy
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi η
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous function
              of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi η
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi Y
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\eta
                    \\;\colon\;
                    X \times [0,1] \longrightarrow Y
                    \\,.
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t \in [0,1]
              write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mi t
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_t
              for the continuous function
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %mphantom
                                  %mi AA
                                %msub
                                  %mi i
                                  %mi t
                                %mphantom
                                  %mi AA
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                            %mo ×
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mn 0
                            %mo ,
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi x
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ↦
                              %mphantom
                                %mi AAAA
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi x
                            %mo ,
                            %mi t
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    X &amp;\overset{\phantom{AA}i_t\phantom{AA}}{\longrightarrow}&amp; X \times [0,1]
                    \\\
                    x &amp;\overset{\phantom{AAAA}}{\mapsto}&amp; (x,t)
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              By the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pasting+law"} pasting law
              for pullbacks we have that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mi E
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi η
                    %mo ∘
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mn 0
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo *
                    %mi E
                    %mo ≃
                    %msubsup
                      %mi i
                      %mn 0
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi η
                      %mo *
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi η
                      %mo *
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo ×
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    f^\ast E = (\eta \circ i_0)^\ast E
                    \\simeq i_0^\ast (\eta^\ast E) \simeq (\eta^\ast E)|_{X \times \{0\}}
            %p and
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi g
                      %mo *
                    %mi E
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi η
                    %mo ∘
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo *
                    %mi E
                    %mo ≃
                    %msubsup
                      %mi i
                      %mn 1
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi η
                      %mo *
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi η
                      %mo *
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo ×
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    g^\ast E = (\eta \circ i_1)^\ast E
                    \\simeq i_1^\ast (\eta^\ast E) \simeq (\eta^\ast E)|_{X \times \{1\}}
            %p
              With this the statement follows by prop.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ConcondanceOfTopologicalVectorBundles"}
          #HomotopyInvarianceOfIsomorphismClassesOfVectorBundles.num_example
            %h6#example_15 Example
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+invariance"} homotopy invariance
                of isomorphism classes of vector bundles)
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              be
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/paracompact+Hausdorff+spaces"} paracompact Hausdorff spaces
              and let
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    f \;\colon\; X \longrightarrow Y
            %p
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous function
              which is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+equivalence"} homotopy equivalence
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              constitutes a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bijection"} bijection
              on sets of isomorphism classes of topological vector bundles:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi Vect
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mo ∼
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mo ≃
                    %mi Vect
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mo ∼
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    f^\ast
                    \\;\colon\;
                    Vect(Y)/_\sim
                    \\overset{\simeq}{\longrightarrow}
                    Vect(X)/_\sim
                    \\,.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_12 Proof
            %p
              By definition of homotopy equivalence, there is a continuous function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g \colon Y \longrightarrow X
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+homotopies"} left homotopies
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi f
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mi id
                    %mphantom
                      %mi AAAA
                    %mi f
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi g
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mi id
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    g \circ f \Rightarrow id
                    \\phantom{AAAA}
                    f \circ g \Rightarrow id
                    \\,.
            %p
              Hence corollary
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PullbackOfvectorBundlesAlongHomotopicMapsAreIsomorphic"}
              implies that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mo ∘
                    %msup
                      %mi g
                      %mo *
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi g
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi f
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo *
                    %mo =
                    %mi id
                    %mphantom
                      %mi AAAAA
                    %msup
                      %mi g
                      %mo *
                    %mo ∘
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi g
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo *
                    %mo =
                    %mi id
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    f^\ast \circ g^\ast = (g \circ f)^\ast = id
                    \\phantom{AAAAA}
                    g^\ast \circ f^\ast = (f \circ g)^\ast = id
                    \\,.
            %p
              This mean that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi g
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g^\ast
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse+function"} inverse function
              to
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^\ast
          #TopologicalVectorBundleOverContractibleSpaceIsTrivializable.num_example
            %h6#example_16 Example
            %p
              %strong (topological vector bundle on contractible topological space is trivializable)
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contractible+topological+space"} contractible topological space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is isomorphic to a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trivial+vector+bundle"} trivial vector bundle
          .proof
            %h6#proof_13 Proof
            %p
              That
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is contractible means by definition that there is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+homotopy"} left homotopy
              of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mo *
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi i
                                  %mn 0
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                            %mo ×
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mn 0
                            %mo ,
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi η
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi i
                                  %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ↗
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi id
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    X &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; \ast
                    \\\
                    \\mathllap{i_0}\downarrow &amp; &amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    X \times [0,1]
                    \&amp;\overset{\eta}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    X
                    \\\
                    \\mathllap{i_1}\uparrow &amp; \nearrow_{\mathrlap{id}}
                    \\\
                    X &amp;
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              By cor
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PullbackOfvectorBundlesAlongHomotopicMapsAreIsomorphic"}
              it follows that for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \to X
              any topological vector bundle that there is an isomorphism between
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi id
                      %mo *
                    %mi E
                    %mo =
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} id^\ast E = E
              and the result of first restricting the bundle to the point, and then forming the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback+bundle"} pullback bundle
              along
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to \ast
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trivial+vector+bundles"} trivial vector bundles
              over
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %h3#OverClosedSubspaces Over closed subspaces
          %p
            We discuss the behavour of vector bundles with respect to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+subspaces"} closed subspaces
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \subset X
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Hausdorff+spaces"} compact Hausdorff spaces
          #IsomorphismOfVectorBundlesOnClosedSubsetOfCompactHausdorffSpaceExtendsToOpenNeighbourhoods.num_lemma
            %h6#lemma_4 Lemma
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
                of vector bundles on
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+subset"} closed subset
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Hausdorff+spaces"} compact Hausdorff spaces
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extension"} extends
                to
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+neighbourhood"} open neighbourhood
            %p
              Let
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo ∈
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ℂ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \in \{\mathbb{R}, \mathbb{C}\}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Hausdorff+space"} compact Hausdorff space
              and let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \subset X
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+subset"} closed
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subspace"} subspace
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mi i
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi p
                          %mi i
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_i \overset{p_i}{\to} X
              be two topological vector bundles over
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo ∈
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \in \{1,2\}
            %p
              If there exists an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi A
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 2
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    E_1\vert_A \overset{\simeq}{\longrightarrow} E_2\vert_A
            %p
              of the restricted vector bundles over
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+subset"} open subset
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \subset X
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \subset U
              such that there is also an isomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi U
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 2
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    E_1\vert_U \overset{\simeq}{\longrightarrow} E_2\vert_U
            %p
              of the vector bundles restricted to
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
          .proof
            %h6#proof_14 Proof
            %p
              A bundle isomorphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi A
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 2
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_1\vert_A \simeq E_2\vert_A
              is equivalently a trivializing section (example
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FiberwiseLinearlyIndependentSectionsTrivialize"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+vector+bundles"} tensor product of vector bundles
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi A
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi A
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 2
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (E_1\vert_A)^\ast \otimes_A E_2\vert_A
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 2
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_2\vert_A
              with the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dual+vector+bundle"} dual vector bundle
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi E
                        %mn 2
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi A
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (E_2\vert_A)^\ast
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "tensor+product+of+vector+bundles#FinitrRankBundleHomomorphismIsSectionOfTensorProductWithDual"} this prop.
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi i
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{V_i \subset X\}_{i \in I}
              be an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+cover"} open cover
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              over which this tensor product bundle trivializes with trivializations
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %msub
                        %mi V
                        %mi i
                      %mo ×
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msup
                            %mi n
                            %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %munderover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mo ≃
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi ϕ
                            %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msubsup
                        %mi E
                        %mn 1
                        %mo *
                      %msub
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi X
                      %msub
                        %mi E
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi U
                            %mi i
                      %mo }
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\left\{
                    V_i \times \mathbb{R}^{(n^2)}
                    \\underoverset{\simeq}{\phi_i}{\longrightarrow}
                    (E_1^\ast \otimes_X E_2)\vert_{U_i}
                    \\right\}
                    \\,.
            %p
              Since
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Hausdorff+spaces+are+normal"} compact Hausdorff spaces are normal
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shrinking+lemma"} shrinking lemma
              applies and gives a refinement of this by a cover
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \subset X\}_{i \in I}
              by
              %em closed
              subsets
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_i \subset X
            %p
              Then a trivializing section
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mi A
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi E
                        %mn 1
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi A
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo *
                      %msub
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi A
                      %msub
                        %mi E
                        %mn 2
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi A
                      %mo )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma \in \Gamma_A\left( (E_1\vert_A)^\ast \otimes_A E_2 \vert_A \right)
              as above is on each
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_i \cap A
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous function
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi σ
                      %mi i
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\sigma_i
                    \\;\colon\;
                    U_i \cap A \longrightarrow GL(n,k)
            %p
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/general+linear+group"} general linear group
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi GL
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo ,
                      %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⊂
                      %msub
                        %mi Mat
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo ×
                          %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL(n,k) \subset Mat_{n \times n}(k)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi i
                        %mo ∩
                        %mi A
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mi i
                    %mo ∘
                    %msub
                      %mi σ
                      %mi i
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\sigma\vert_{U_i \cap A} = \phi_i \circ \sigma_i
                    \\,.
            %p
              Regarded as a function to the
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ×
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \times n
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/matrices"} matrices
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi n
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n^2
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi σ
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ((\sigma_i)_{a b})
            %p
              Now since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_i \subset X
              is closed by construction, and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \subset X
              is closed by assumption, also the intersections
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_i \cap X
              are closed. Since
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Hausdorff+spaces+are+normal"} compact Hausdorff spaces are normal
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tietze+extension+theorem"} Tietze extension theorem
              therefore applies to these component functions and yields
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extensions"} extensions
              of each
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
